<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Parma</h1><p class="st-meta">1149 CE – 1346 CE (approx.) · capital Parma</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Emilian city-republic that defeated Emperor Frederick II's siege in 1248 and commissioned Benedetto Antelami's great baptistery.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Parma's citizens gradually took power from their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, who had been counts of the city, and by 1149 consuls governed the commune. It controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/via-aemilia">Via Emilia</a> and a route across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Tuscany</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governed by consuls, then a podestà and popular councils, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Parma</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a>. In 1196 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benedetto-antelami">Benedetto Antelami</a> began its octagonal baptistery. Ghibelline at first, it turned Guelph in 1247 and withstood Frederick II's siege, destroying his camp-city of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-victoria">Victoria</a> in February 1248. The Rossi, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-correggio">Correggio</a> and Sanvitale families competed for power; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giberto-da-correggio">Giberto da Correggio</a> became lord in 1303.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After a succession of lords, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obizzo-iii-deste">Obizzo III d'Este</a> sold the city to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luchino-visconti-lord-of-milan">Luchino Visconti</a> in 1346, and it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a>. In 1545 it became the capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1149 CE – 1346 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.57%;width:3.92%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1149 CE – 1346 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Parma</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Giberto da Correggio</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Emilian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Italy</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Parma</dd></dl></aside></div>

